64
00:05:46,613 --> 00:05:49,613
Presenting, building circles, yay!

65
00:05:49,613 --> 00:05:56,613
So you're going to want to start out with this sort of graph paper, just trace something circular onto it, and then fill in the blocks that the circle cross.

66
00:05:56,613 --> 00:05:58,613
Make sure it all has the same radius.

67
00:05:58,613 --> 00:06:00,613
And then this is where the calculus comes in.

68
00:06:00,613 --> 00:06:04,613
If you look at tangent lines, you know what tangent lines are, I hope.

69
00:06:04,613 --> 00:06:06,653
You probably don't.

70
00:06:06,653 --> 00:06:14,653
But the slope of the tangent line is sort of the slope of if you were to draw the slope through the grid squares of the circle.

71
00:06:14,653 --> 00:06:16,653
This made a lot more sense inside my head.

72
00:06:16,653 --> 00:06:22,653
But you can trace pretty much any circle on the graph paper and repeat this process.

73
00:06:22,653 --> 00:06:26,093
Just make sure the radius is the same and that each quadrant is the same.

74
00:06:26,093 --> 00:06:28,653
And there you go, you have a circle in Minecraft.

